    en: { title: "Qualification, certification or designation — what is the difference?", summary: "CIPS, CPSM, MCIPS, MBA: understand what each credential actually is before you invest.",
      body: `People often use these words as if they mean the same thing. They do not.

## Qualification
A course of study with an assessed result, often in levels. *Example: CIPS Level 4 Diploma, an MBA.*

## Certification
An exam-based credential that proves knowledge at a point in time, often with renewal rules. *Example: ISM CPSM, ASCM CSCP, PMI PMP.*

## Professional designation
A title granted by a professional body, usually after a qualification **plus** relevant experience and a code of conduct. *Example: MCIPS.*

## Which matters most?
It depends on your stage and employers. Look at real job ads in your target industry and count what they ask for. No credential guarantees a promotion or a salary increase — but the right one, combined with results, helps you get shortlisted.

Compare options with the **Certification Comparison Tool** in Career Tools.` },
